# Authentication — JWT + Refresh Tokens

Admin-only authentication. Login by `username` (not email). Follows the standard module layout (domain → application → infrastructure).

## Stack

- `@nestjs/jwt` + `@nestjs/passport` + `passport-jwt` for access tokens.
- `@nestjs/schedule` for the refresh-token cleanup CRON.
- `bcrypt` via shared `IHasher` (`src/common/security/hasher.interface.ts`) — used for both admin passwords and refresh-token secrets.
- `cookie-parser` registered in `main.ts` (required to read the refresh cookie).

## Token rules

| Token | TTL | Storage |
|---|---|---|
| Access token (JWT) | `JWT_ACCESS_EXPIRES_IN` (default `15m`) | `Authorization: Bearer <token>` header |
| Refresh token (opaque) | `REFRESH_TOKEN_TTL_HOURS` (default `48`) | `refresh_token` cookie (`httpOnly`, `sameSite: strict`) |

JWT payload: `{ sub: adminId, username }`. Strategy `validate()` returns `ICurrentUser` `{ id, username }` consumed by `@CurrentUser()`.

## Refresh token format

Opaque cookie value: `"{id}.{secret}"`.

| Part | Source | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `id` | UUID — PK of the whitelist row | Indexed lookup via `findById` |
| `secret` | `randomBytes(32).toString('hex')` | Only its bcrypt hash is persisted in `tokenHash` |

Encode/decode lives in `application/utils/refresh-token-codec.util.ts` (`buildRawRefreshToken`, `parseRawRefreshToken`).

## Whitelist (`admin_refresh_tokens`)

- **One row per login**, not per user. Multiple concurrent sessions are allowed.
- Persisted fields: `tokenHash` (bcrypt of secret), `userAgent`, `expiresAt`, `adminId`. No `updated_at` — rows are created on login and deleted on logout/rotation; never updated.
- On **refresh**: validate → delete old row → create new row **reusing the previous `expiresAt`** (session never extends past the original login window) → set new cookie (rotation).
- On **logout**: delete row by `id` parsed from cookie; idempotent (missing/malformed cookie is not an error).
- On **secret mismatch** (known `id`, wrong secret): delete the row immediately (possible token theft) and reject.
- On **expired token**: delete if the row exists, then reject.
- **CRON** (`RefreshTokenCleanupJob`, `@Cron(CronExpression.EVERY_HOUR)`): calls `deleteExpired()` on the repository.

Domain entity: `AdminRefreshToken` (`domain/entities/admin-refresh-token.entity.ts`).
Repository token: `ADMIN_REFRESH_TOKEN_REPOSITORY` → `IAdminRefreshTokenRepository` (`save`, `findById`, `deleteById`, `deleteExpired`).

## Endpoints

All return `ApiResponseDto<T>` with a specific `message` (never the generic default). Errors are thrown from use cases only.

| Method | Path | Guard | Responsibility |
|---|---|---|---|
| `POST` | `/api/auth/login` | — | Authenticate admin, issue access token + set refresh cookie |
| `POST` | `/api/auth/refresh` | — | Validate cookie against whitelist, rotate refresh token, issue new access token |
| `DELETE` | `/api/auth/logout` | `JwtAuthGuard` | Delete whitelist row, clear cookie |

Controller: `infrastructure/http/auth.controller.ts`. Zero logic — delegates to use cases, sets/clears cookie, wraps in `ApiResponseDto.ok`.

## Required pieces

| Piece | Location | Responsibility |
|---|---|---|
| `LoginUseCase` | `application/use-cases/login/login.use-case.ts` | Validates credentials via `IAdminRepository` + `IHasher`; creates whitelist row; signs JWT |
| `RefreshTokenUseCase` | `application/use-cases/refresh-token/refresh-token.use-case.ts` | Parses cookie, validates + rotates whitelist row, signs new JWT |
| `LogoutUseCase` | `application/use-cases/logout/logout.use-case.ts` | Idempotent whitelist row deletion |
| `RefreshTokenCleanupJob` | `application/jobs/refresh-token-cleanup.job.ts` | Hourly purge of expired rows |
| `JwtStrategy` | `infrastructure/passport/jwt.strategy.ts` | Validates Bearer access token; populates `req.user` |
| `JwtAuthGuard` | `infrastructure/guards/jwt-auth.guard.ts` | Protects routes (`AuthGuard('jwt')`) |
| `@CurrentUser()` | `infrastructure/decorators/current-user.decorator.ts` | Extracts `ICurrentUser` from `req.user` |
| `AUTH_MESSAGES` | `application/constants/auth-messages.constants.ts` | Centralized success/error messages (Spanish) |

## Response messages

Import from `AUTH_MESSAGES` — never hardcode strings in use cases, controller, or tests.

| Case | Message |
|---|---|
| Login success | `"Usuario logueado con éxito"` |
| Invalid credentials | `"Usuario o contraseña incorrectos"` (same message whether username or password is wrong) |
| Refresh success | `"Token renovado con éxito"` |
| Invalid/malformed cookie | `"Sesión inválida, por favor inicia sesión nuevamente"` |
| Expired / not found / secret mismatch | `"Sesión expirada, por favor inicia sesión nuevamente"` |
| Logout success | `"Sesión cerrada con éxito"` |

## Cookie setup

```typescript
res.cookie('refresh_token', rawRefreshToken, {
  httpOnly: true,
  sameSite: 'strict',
  secure: configService.get('NODE_ENV') === 'production',
  expires: expiresAt, // absolute date from the whitelist row — never recalculated on refresh
});
```

## Whitelist entity (reference)

```typescript
@Entity('admin_refresh_tokens')
export class AdminRefreshTokenTypeOrmEntity {
  @PrimaryColumn('uuid')
  id: string;

  @Column({ name: 'token_hash', type: 'varchar', length: 255 })
  tokenHash: string;       // bcrypt hash of the secret (NOT the full cookie value)

  @Column({ name: 'user_agent', type: 'varchar', length: 255 })
  userAgent: string;

  @Column({ name: 'expires_at', type: 'timestamp' })
  expiresAt: Date;

  @CreateDateColumn({ name: 'created_at', type: 'timestamp' })
  createdAt: Date;

  @Column({ name: 'admin_id', type: 'uuid' })
  adminId: string;
}
```

## Module wiring

`AuthModule` imports: `AdminModule` (for `ADMIN_REPOSITORY`), `PassportModule`, `ScheduleModule.forRoot()`, `TypeOrmModule.forFeature([AdminRefreshTokenTypeOrmEntity])`, `JwtModule.registerAsync` (secret/expiry from `ConfigService`).

Providers: repository binding, `HASHER` → `BcryptHasherImpl`, all use cases, `JwtStrategy`, `RefreshTokenCleanupJob`.

## Environment variables

| Variable | Default | Used by |
|---|---|---|
| `JWT_ACCESS_SECRET` | — (required) | `JwtModule`, `JwtStrategy` |
| `JWT_ACCESS_EXPIRES_IN` | `15m` | `JwtModule.signOptions.expiresIn` |
| `REFRESH_TOKEN_TTL_HOURS` | `48` | Login use case only (refresh inherits previous `expiresAt`; cookie uses absolute `expires`) |
| `NODE_ENV` | — | Cookie `secure` flag (`production` → `true`) |
